# Claude
# AGENTS.md (canonical entry file) + CLAUDE.md (its one-line @AGENTS.md stub) + the module
# CLAUDE.md files are COMMITTED — shared, public-safe agent instructions (ADR-021).
# Personal/transient notes go in CLAUDE.local.md (gitignored).
# ALL of .claude/ is local working state (ADR-029, 2026-07-25): CONTEXT.md, KNOWN_ISSUES.md and
# RIGOR_TODO.md left the allowlist with the second machine. ADR-020 committed RIGOR_TODO.md purely
# to converge two boxes' disjoint copies; with one box git is not a sync mechanism, only a
# publication channel, and these files are addressed to the builder, not to a reader of a public
# repo. AGENTS.md's digest is what an out-of-clone reader gets; see docs/local-only.md.
# ⚠ Consequence: nothing here has an off-machine copy any more — back up .claude/ yourself.
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/
# Rotated-out baton entries (cpc rotation, ADR-018 rule 11) — local-only, like the baton itself.
docs/archive/SESSION-archive-*.md
# Working docs, local-only for the same reason (ADR-029): dated planning docs, review reports and
# the UI punch list are working notes, not the project's public record (which is README · ADRs ·
# specs · DEVLOG · ROADMAP). Committed docs still link to them — docs/local-only.md explains why
# those links don't resolve in a clone.
docs/PLAN_*.md
docs/REVIEW_*.md
docs/ui-checklist.md
# Local-only convention gates that depend on a private tooling repo — never shared (see ADR-001).
.pre-commit-config.cpc.yaml
tools/conventions/

# Runtime data
# settings.json is the app's persisted per-machine settings (provider/model selection, U1c) —
# written by the app at runtime, never committed (it would pin one user's choice for everyone).
data/settings.json
